[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1752","stub":{"id":"1752","section":"1. Dries: Turtletown Creek to Apalachia Powerhouse ","altname":"Dries","river":"Hiwassee","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-TNN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"hazard","description":"This goes on and on and on for about 3 miles.","id":"1080","location":{"latitude":"35.168067932128906","longitude":"-84.31661224365234"},"name":"Don't put in at Hwy 68","distance":"-3.4","photoID":"4713","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":"The better access point.","id":"1090","location":{"latitude":"35.17010498046875","longitude":"-84.36519622802734"},"name":"Turtletown Creek","distance":"0","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"waterfall","description":"A multi ledge rapid with any number of routes. The picture shows the bottom half of the rapid. There is a similar sized ledge in the background. After running this ledge, there is a fast run out thru a couple of holes.","id":"1081","location":{"latitude":"35.17768096923828","longitude":"-84.38030242919922"},"name":"Hollywood Bowl (First Rapid)","distance":"1","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"4714"},{"type":"hazard","description":"This rapid is rather long with several pools and ledges. Note that there is a terrible pothole sieve to the paddlers left in this picture (the right side of the main channel). Stay on the high ramp and do not get into the slot to the left or especially to the left of the slot. You can also run down the left of the main channel which is often more of a big water line.","id":"1096","location":{"latitude":"35.177345","longitude":"-84.379167"},"name":"Hollywood Bowl","distance":"1","photoID":"4716","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":"A 4-car pull out here allows access down a steep roped trail to the river, just downstream of Hollywood Bowl. The road is fine for most/all vehicles. Park shortly after the road turns away from Wolf Creek.","id":"qavCrclwGuuMrv5o53e2J","location":{"latitude":"35.173774","longitude":"-84.384135"},"name":"Standard (Wolf Creek) Put In","distance":"1.41","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"A long western style wave train with some hidden holes. At the bottom was a 10 foot tall boulder. At this level the guys coming down in the back of the pack were able to boof off the rock. Those of us who probed it were afraid it was going to make a huge hole. With a bit more water this rock would make a huge riverwide hole.","id":"1087","location":{"latitude":"35.17368698120117","longitude":"-84.38811492919922"},"name":"Wu (Second Rapid )","distance":"1.5","photoID":"4776","difficulty":"III+","approximate":true},{"type":"playspot","description":"Long cool wavetrain rapid. Big waves. Lots of surfing.","id":"1088","location":{"latitude":"35.176300048828125","longitude":"-84.39640045166016"},"name":"Long Wave Train","distance":"2.8","difficulty":"II+","approximate":true,"photoID":"4777"},{"type":"rapid","description":"The narrows starts by punching a large hole. This is more interesting because both walls appeared to be undercut. Then you have a half mile of cliffed out swirly boiling water. Expect the unexpected. This water tried to stern squirt a Prijon Tornado a couple of times. Or just see the classic Neely cartoon of funny water.","id":"1089","location":{"latitude":"35.18107986450195","longitude":"-84.40896606445312"},"name":"The Narrows","distance":"3.5","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Most people take out on river left just downstream of the Apalachia powerhouse, parking out of the way in the gravel lot near the river, and of course outside of the gates to the powerhouse. A gate at the top of the gorge is sometimes locked, sometimes not. Other folks choose to take out at the Lower Hiwassee put in, downstream. A foot bridge here provide hiking access across the river.","id":"118068","location":{"latitude":"35.1833","longitude":"-84.438797"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"5.5","photoID":"888833","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"PlrmSbR6tfh5QlbePXJ97","title":"Dries to Spill 1600 over this weekend","post_date":"2022-12-15 18:48:58+00","detail":"TVA has announced that the Hiwassee Dries will begin running at around 1600 cfs today (12/15/22) and will continue running over the weekend and into early next week.","user":{"name":"Kevin Colburn"}},{"id":"101254547","title":null,"post_date":"2020-02-19 05:00:00+00","detail":"5600 cfs release at least through this weekend (2/19/20)","user":{"name":"Kevin Colburn"}},{"id":"101252754","title":null,"post_date":"2016-12-01 05:00:00+00","detail":"I have run this section lots of times. 7000+-cfs being the highest and 550cfs being the lowest. At both levels this is a very runable and fun run. At the higher levels 4000-6500 there is a very good play wave right before coker creek comes in with eddie service. ( At all levels a play boat is fine ) Hollywood bowl has a large tree at bottom of main drop right now that should be scouted at higher levels. I would say 4500+ this run is closer to a class five run even though a class five boater will have no issues. I have seen a few walk out after reading all this stuff above and going in at a high level. At the 550 - 2500 range the river is very friendly and i think all beginners could take a stab at it.","user":{"name":"Jonathan \"sprayer\" Campbell"}}],"photos":[{"id":"50621","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"153579","description":"taking a risk that I didnt tip, I grabbed the camera in the middle of this class 2","caption":"in the middle of the rapids","poi_name":"Not sure, after stairsteps, before funnel..","subject":"Barry, you just cant see him !","author":"Barry","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50621","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50621"}},{"id":"4776","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1388","description":"Long wavetrain with a Huge rock bisecting the bottom.  Eddylines on both sides were interesting.  At higher flows this would make a riverwide hole.  Some of our guys boofed off the rock after we found out the bottom was clear.  There is a boater in the pic on the left side of the rock","caption":"2nd Rapid on the Drys","poi_name":"2nd big rapid","subject":"Eric Paysen","author":"Kevin Miller","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4776","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4776"}},{"id":"891873","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895782","description":null,"caption":"Katie Schmidt","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891873","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891873"}},{"id":"SaYPGqLckOn959rtZaB0v","ext":"jpg","post_id":"1uGiRyYOYNKAsIGYmYHFr","description":"Looking back upstream after stopping on mid stream rock to scout Hollywood Bowl Rapid. This rock is river right near the center, fairly easy to find at this flow (1500ish) Stopping here gives good views of various lines through the upper tiers of the rapid, and you can spot the best line through the main drop, although you cannot see the runout afterwards. There are more eddies below here, and in particular a brushy one on river right that is easy to access and scout/ set safety/portage the main drop.\nThis is a great place to regroup before dropping in. As on 08/09/2022 there is bad wood in the left bottom of Hollywood Bowl, and scouting from the railroad tracks can prove more difficult during the summer months when the leaves are blocking easy views ","caption":"Hollywood Bowl Scout Rock","poi_name":null,"subject":"Hollywood Bowl Scout Rock","author":"Matthew Haughee","poi_id":"1096","photo_date":"2022-08-09T19:54:04.000Z","updated_at":"2022-08-10T19:54:04.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/SaYPGqLckOn959rtZaB0v","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/SaYPGqLckOn959rtZaB0v"}},{"id":"3n0b9BBjJ3liocx2wVt6e","ext":"jpg","post_id":"1uGiRyYOYNKAsIGYmYHFr","description":"Second Major Rapid. Easy to read and run at this level. Comes around what feels like a half mile below Wolf Creek. The large rock at the bottom of the rapid turns into a pourover at higher flow!","caption":"Second Major Rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":"Look at that sky!","author":"Matthew Haughee","poi_id":"1087","photo_date":"2022-08-09T19:54:04.000Z","updated_at":"2022-08-10T19:54:04.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3n0b9BBjJ3liocx2wVt6e","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3n0b9BBjJ3liocx2wVt6e"}},{"id":"fzUp4sAOhDssfi2Dm8N0k","ext":"jpg","post_id":"1uGiRyYOYNKAsIGYmYHFr","description":"Just downstream of the paddler, the right wall provides views of some very interesting boils, and the more water through here the more interesting they look ","caption":"Narrows ","poi_name":null,"subject":"Jared Dempsey","author":"Matthew Haughee","poi_id":"1089","photo_date":"2022-08-09T19:54:04.000Z","updated_at":"2022-08-10T19:54:04.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/fzUp4sAOhDssfi2Dm8N0k","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/fzUp4sAOhDssfi2Dm8N0k"}},{"id":"GDgJonILFXeNCnUoP1j6R","ext":"jpg","post_id":"M5KlNy4SuGtvRTW99u2kQ","description":"The wolf creek put in requires a short steep descent. ","caption":"The put in \"Trail\"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"qavCrclwGuuMrv5o53e2J","photo_date":"2016-02-06T18:03:56.000Z","updated_at":"2022-07-18T18:03:57.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/med